{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The issue was in `percentile` in `repo/stats.py`, which feeds report summaries via `summarize()` in `repo/aggregate.py` (p50, p90, p99).\n\n**Cause:** The rank used `int(p / 100 * n)`, which truncates toward zero. Nearest-rank percentiles need a ceiling: the value at rank `ceil(p/100 × n)` (1-based). Truncation picks the next higher value (e.g. p50 on 1…10 gave **6** instead of **5**). At p=100, `int(n)` is index `n`, which is out of range.\n\n**Fix:** Compute `rank = ceil(p/100 × n)` and use index `rank - 1`, clamped to `[0, n - 1]`, so p=0 is the minimum and p=100 is the maximum as documented.\n\nAll visible tests pass."}]},"session_id":"8ebb1c25-ba98-431f-9566-3af71c57975d"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":44038,"duration_api_ms":44038,"is_error":false,"result":"Searching the codebase for how report percentiles are calculated and displayed.\n\n\nRunning tests to confirm the bug:\n\n\nFixing nearest-rank percentile: use `ceil(p/100 * n) - 1` instead of truncating with `int()`.\n\n\nThe issue was in `percentile` in `repo/stats.py`, which feeds report summaries via `summarize()` in `repo/aggregate.py` (p50, p90, p99).\n\n**Cause:** The rank used `int(p / 100 * n)`, which truncates toward zero. Nearest-rank percentiles need a ceiling: the value at rank `ceil(p/100 × n)` (1-based). Truncation picks the next higher value (e.g. p50 on 1…10 gave **6** instead of **5**). At p=100, `int(n)` is index `n`, which is out of range.\n\n**Fix:** Compute `rank = ceil(p/100 × n)` and use index `rank - 1`, clamped to `[0, n - 1]`, so p=0 is the minimum and p=100 is the maximum as documented.\n\nAll visible tests pass.","session_id":"8ebb1c25-ba98-431f-9566-3af71c57975d","request_id":"ba150bef-d237-48a6-ba28-955cb6fa2396","usage":{"inputTokens":12097,"outputTokens":2040,"cacheReadTokens":81472,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
